00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:25.340
Yeah, there's, I mean, and we were also like,
是的，我的意思是，而且我们当时还……

298
00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:28.060
they made a thing that tilted, right?
他们做了一个会倾斜的东西，对吧？

299
00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:28.900
Yes, they did.
是的，他们做了。

300
00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:29.740
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

301
00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:32.260
But you also did some clever camera work in moments too, right?
不过你们在某些镜头里也运用了很巧妙的运镜，对吧？

302
00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:36.900
We did, but that entire set was lifted off the ground
确实如此，但整个布景当时是被整个吊离地面

303
00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:38.340
and pitched.
然后倾斜的。

304
00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:39.340
Yeah.
对。

305
00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:41.060
Like we probably told you guys that idea
这个创意我们大概在

306
00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:42.460
about a week ahead of time.
提前一周左右就跟你们说过。

307
00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:44.540
And then it's like, you build up this whole set
然后就变成了，你们搭建了这样一个完整布景

308
00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:46.860
on a giant winch that tilts.
在一个会倾斜的巨大绞盘上。

309
00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:47.900
And they're like, all right,
然后他们就说，好吧，

310
00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:51.700
there was such a challenge accepted aesthetic on that set.
那个剧组当时有一种欣然接受挑战的审美氛围。

311
00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.100
I mean, that's probably why that became
我的意思是，这大概也就是为什么那句话后来成了

312
00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:54.180
one of Barney's things he said.
巴尼的标志性台词之一。

313
00:14:54.180 --> 00:14:57.100
Cause that was just the ethos of the crew.
因为那就是整个剧组的精神风貌。

314
00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:58.540
You were the head of them and you,
你是他们的负责人，而且你，

315
00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:00.380
you all, you're getting carted on a credit.
你们大家，你在职员工名单里都被署名了。

316
00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:02.420
You very much set that tone.
很大程度上是你定下了这种基调。

317
00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:05.380
And in the way where everyone wanted to accept
在那种人人都想接受

318
00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:07.580
that challenge and nail it for you,
这个挑战并为你把它干漂亮的氛围下，

319
00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:08.420
you asked them to do it.
你要求他们这么做。

320
00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:09.980
They wanted to do it for you.
他们是发自内心地想为你这么做。

321
00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:12.780
You know, I am in my first film,
你知道的，我当时在拍我的第一部电影，

322
00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:15.180
which I hadn't yet directed at this point.
而且我当时还没执导过电影。

323
00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:16.420
Happy, thank you more, please.
《开心就好，谢谢，再多来点》。

324
00:15:16.420 --> 00:15:17.980
I directed it in between our first,
我是趁着我们拍第一季，

325
00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:19.660
a fourth and fifth season.
第四季和第五季的间隙执导的。

326
00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:22.580
And we had a production meeting where we had to figure out
我们当时开了一个制作会议，得研究

327
00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:24.460
New York taxi cabs, when we can get it.
纽约的出租车，什么时候能弄到。

328
00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:25.860
Oh, it's in front of a police station.
哦，是在一个警察局门前。

329
00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:29.060
You're not allowed to show a precinct number in a TV,
你在电视剧里是不能展示警局编号的，

330
00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:30.300
like in a movie.
就像在电影里一样。

331
00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:31.420
Like there were all these things.
诸如此类的事情有一大堆。

332
00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:34.380
And my DP saw my face kind of turn white.
我的摄影指导看到我的脸当时有点吓白了。

333
00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:35.780
And he pulled me aside afterwards.
事后他把我拉到一边。

334
00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:36.620
He goes, what's going on?
他问，怎么了？

335
00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:37.460
I said, I'm terrified.
我说，我快吓死了。

336
00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:38.300
Cause we were starting on Monday.
因为我们周一就要开机了。

337
00:15:38.300 --> 00:15:39.660
This is like a Friday.
这大概是周五的时候。

338
00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:41.980
And I said, he said, what are you afraid of?
然后我说，他说，你在怕什么？

339
00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:44.380
I said, I'm afraid people are going to be asking me questions
我说，我怕大家会不停地

340
00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:44.829
constantly.
问我各种问题。

341
00:15:44.829 --> 00:15:46.340
I'm not going to know the answers to.
而我都不知道答案。

342
00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:50.540
And he said, you make a film to figure out the answers.
然后他说，你拍电影就是为了找出答案。

343
00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:52.500
You don't know the answers beforehand.
你不可能事先就知道所有答案。

344
00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:55.420
Every day you show up with problems to solve.
你每天到现场都是带着要解决的问题来的。

345
00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:56.860
And you solve them one by one.
然后你把它们逐一解决掉。

346
00:15:56.860 --> 00:15:58.300
That's what making a movie is.
拍电影就是这么回事。

347
00:15:58.300 --> 00:16:03.300
And I feel like that's what making any TV show is like,
我觉得拍任何电视剧也是一样的，

348
00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:06.500
the script is like a problem to be solved.
剧本就像是一个待解决的问题。

349
00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:10.260
Like you hand them like, oh, a crooked apartment.
就像你递给他们一个，哦，一个歪斜的公寓。

350
00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:11.780
Like that's tilted.
就像那种倾斜的布景。

351
00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.940
Like, how are we going to do that?
话说回来，我们要怎么做到这一点呢？

352
00:16:13.940 --> 00:16:15.140
But there was, like you said,
但正如你所说的那样，

353
00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:16.620
like a very challenged accepted thing.
这就像是一场“接受挑战”的豪言壮语。

354
00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.820
Like I remember sometimes, I'm like,
就像我有时会想，

355
00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:20.820
I don't know if you ever were freaked out,
我不知道你是不是曾经也被吓坏过，

356
00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:22.420
but you certainly didn't show it.
但你确实一点也没表现出来。

357
00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:24.380
You know, and I think that you,
你知道的，我觉得你，

358
00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:27.140
I don't know, there was just a very can-do attitude
怎么说呢，对于所有那些疯狂的事情，

359
00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:28.340
about all the insane things.
你都抱着一种“绝对能搞定”的态度。

360
00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:30.180
And here's a question, 18 years later.
所以有个问题，18年后的今天，

361
00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:31.340
Were you freaked out?
你当时害怕吗？

362
00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:32.180
Yeah, were you?
对啊，你害怕吗？

363
00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:37.220
I'm in the white man moment or two,
我有过那么一两次慌乱的时刻，

364
00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:40.820
but to your point Josh, I will tell you
但正如你所说的小乔，我想告诉你的是，

365
00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:45.020
that when I talk to young people coming up,
每当我跟刚出道的年轻人交流时，

366
00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:48.260
one of the best things I can say to them
我能对他们说的最好的一点就是，

367
00:16:48.260 --> 00:16:51.660
is the biggest mistake a director makes going on stage
导演上台时犯的最大错误，

368
00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:54.460
is thinking they have to know everything.
就是以为自己必须无所不知。

369
00:16:54.460 --> 00:16:57.780
And the beauty is getting on that stage
而最美妙的是走上那个舞台，

370
00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:01.700
and talking to all of those experts
跟所有的专家们交流，

371
00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:04.460
and figuring, you know, here's what I'm thinking.
然后琢磨着，你看，我是这么想的，

372
00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.340
What do you think?
你们觉得呢？

373
00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:09.580
And on that stage specifically saying,
而且在那个特定的舞台上说，

374
00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:11.540
here's what I'm thinking, what do you think
我是这么想的，你们觉得呢，

375
00:17:11.540 --> 00:17:14.380
was the greatest thing in the world?
这简直是世界上最棒的事了，

376
00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:17.100
Because everybody had valuable information.
因为每个人都有宝贵的信息。

377
00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:20.700
Because you're also like, you're surrounded by the top people,
因为你也会觉得，你被顶尖的人才环绕着，

378
00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:23.180
you're surrounded by the top people in every field.
你被每个领域的顶尖人物环绕着。

379
00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:25.180
Why wouldn't you crowdsource the best idea?
为什么不通过众包来集思广益最好的点子呢？

380
00:17:25.180 --> 00:17:26.500
Exactly.
完全正确。

381
00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:28.460
Exactly, exactly.
完全正确，确实如此。

382
00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:31.340
But I understand that when you get that job,
但我理解当你得到那份工作时，

383
00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:33.820
you think, I has to know everything.
你会想，我必须无所不知。

384
00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:35.620
Like, this is my job now.
就像，这就是我现在的职责。

385
00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:39.660
And you're terrified and you realize that when you walk on
然后你感到恐惧，接着你意识到当你走上台，

386
00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:42.340
and you ask a question, people are so happy
提出一个问题时，大家是多么高兴

387
00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:45.340
to be part of the process.
能成为这个过程的一部分。

388
00:17:45.340 --> 00:17:48.900
Yeah, and everyone wants to be a part of something good.
对啊，每个人都想成为美好事物的一部分。

389
00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:49.740
Yes.
没错。

390
00:17:49.820 --> 00:17:51.780
Like, everyone wants it to be good.
就像，每个人都希望成果是完美的。

391
00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:53.620
Like, you want to have fun on set,
就像，你希望在片场过得开心，

392
00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:56.220
but not if the final product isn't great.
但前提是最终的作品必须足够出色。

393
00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:57.780
Because then you're never going to see each other again.
因为否则你们就再也不会合作了。

394
00:17:57.780 --> 00:18:00.820
If you make something great, you can keep doing it.
如果你做出了伟大的作品，你们就能一直合作下去。

395
00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:04.100
To me, the perfect example of that was the two-minute date.
对我来说，最完美的例子就是那个两分钟的约会。

396
00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:07.260
Also, in this back nine whirlwind game show, Batch.
还有，在这场后半程的旋风式游戏节目里，Batch。

397
00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:08.740
I mean, when one, yeah.
我是说，当某人，对吧。

398
00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:13.980
And what you saw behind the cameras was incredible.
而且你在镜头背后看到的情景简直难以置信。

399
00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:16.100
And everybody having the greatest time
每个人都玩得超级开心，

400
00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:19.180
and saying, I'll do this, you do this, you do this.
并且互相配合着说：“我来做这个，你做那个，他负责这个。”

401
00:18:19.180 --> 00:18:20.340
And it's a team sport.
而且这是一项团队运动。

402
00:18:20.340 --> 00:18:24.060
I mean, it's to just, that's how we did all of these.
我的意思是，这就，我们所有这些都是这么拍的。

403
00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:26.220
We talked to Sarah talk about this, Pam,
我们和莎拉谈过这个，帕姆，

404
00:18:26.220 --> 00:18:28.300
and that was another one I missed having you on.
这也是我遗憾没能让你参与的另一集。

405
00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:29.540
We should have had you and Sarah on.
我们本该让你和莎拉都参与进来的。

406
00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:30.380
I love you so.
我太爱你了。

407
00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:32.580
But just to talk about it, we're trying this episode
但我们就着这个聊聊，我们在尝试这一集

408
00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:34.260
of this season three recap episode.
第三季的回顾集。

409
00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:36.180
We're just jumping around.
我们只是随性闲聊。

410
00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:37.300
But what is your remember?
但你有什么记忆？

411
00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:39.900
Just for people who don't immediately know what you mean.
为了让大家不至于一下子明白你的意思。

412
00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:42.180
Two-minute date, it was all one shot for two minutes.
两分钟的约会，整整两分钟都是一个长镜头。

413
00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:44.700
It was Ted taking Sarah Josh Carter's song.
那是泰德采用了莎拉·乔希·卡特的歌。

414
00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:48.340
One giant, very intricate, all these moving parts.
一个巨大的、非常复杂的、所有这些都在移动的场景。

415
00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:50.380
What is your memory of what that looked like,
在你记忆中，那看起来是什么样的，

416
00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:53.500
not to the camera lens, but to you, but standing there?
不是通过摄像机镜头，而是对你而言，就站在那里？

417
00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:57.500
Yeah, it was what was happening right outside of the lens.
对，就是镜头外面正在发生的事。

418
00:18:57.500 --> 00:19:01.420
It was what was happening when you went by that restaurant
那是当你走过那家餐厅时发生的事，

419
00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:04.180
and they ran in and redressed that restaurant
他们跑进去重新布置了那家餐厅，

420
00:19:04.180 --> 00:19:07.780
while we were down, like people were working so fast
在我们休息的时候，大家工作得太快了，

421
00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:12.580
and so hard to get things ready as the camera was, oh.
为了在镜头转到时把一切准备好，真是太拼了，哦。

422
00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:15.260
And athletically, like, like, you know,
而且在运动方面，就像，你知道的，

423
00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:18.260
crouching and moving and, like,
蹲下、移动，还有，

424
00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:19.420
because they had to stay out of frame.
因为他们必须避开画幅。

425
00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:20.260
Yeah.
是的。

426
00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:21.420
Sarah said she felt relaxed, those.
莎拉说她当时感觉很放松，那些。

427
00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:24.380
Pam, you had a set where this cast could be happening.
帕姆，你们那个片场能让这种演员阵容的戏发生。

428
00:19:24.380 --> 00:19:26.820
I think Sarah gave you the credit, or like she and Josh
我想莎拉把功劳归于你了，或者她和乔希

429
00:19:26.820 --> 00:19:30.580
had this, like, memory of not feeling hurried
有这样一种记忆：并没有感到催促，

430
00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:32.500
because everything was moving so fast around them.
因为周围的一切都移动得非常快。

431
00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:34.380
But they were, like, in the eye of the hurricane,
但他们就像是处在飓风眼，

432
00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:36.460
the eye of the store, and they were, like, the center.
暴风眼的中心，而他们就是核心。

433
00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:39.460
And we got to be, like, part of their ginger rogers
而我们得以成为他们身边的舞伴，

434
00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:43.220
in the middle of that, they were, like, really relaxed.
在风暴中央，他们表现得真的很放松。

435
00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:44.660
It plays relaxed.
呈现出来的效果很放松。

436
00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:46.500
That's how it plays, even though it's not,
效果就是这样，尽管事实并非如此，

437
00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:49.540
it's not like the sport is happening just off camera.
就好像运动就在镜头外发生着。

438
00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:50.380
Yeah.
是的。

439
00:19:50.380 --> 00:19:52.940
Well, my memory is, I mean, we certainly did it a few times,
嗯，我的记忆是，我的意思是，我们确实拍了好几次，

440
00:19:52.940 --> 00:19:54.700
but it didn't take forever, like, we got it.
但也没有没完没了，我们最后搞定了。

441
00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:56.180
I think we did three.
我想我们拍了三次。

442
00:19:56.180 --> 00:19:57.180
Yeah, I think we did three times.
对，我想我们拍了三次。

443
00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:58.860
I think we did three, and I think you used take two
我想我们拍了三次，如果我没记错的话，

444
00:19:58.860 --> 00:19:59.700
as my memory.
你们用了第二条。

445
00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:00.540
Maybe.
也许吧。

446
00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:02.620
But I could, I could be wrong.
不过我也可能记错。

447
00:20:02.620 --> 00:20:05.740
Magic, and magic and teamwork.
奇迹，奇迹与团队合作。

448
00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:08.500
I mean, fun for Sue, she just has to pick one take.
我的意思是，对苏来说挺轻松的，她只需要挑一条就行。

449
00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:10.860
In fact, I would not say it's only a magic, Pam.
事实上，帕姆，我不会说这只是个奇迹，

450
00:20:10.860 --> 00:20:13.260
I would say it was a miracle,
我要说这是一个神迹，

451
00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:15.260
which brings us back to this episode,
这把我们带回了这一集，

452
00:20:15.260 --> 00:20:16.900
which is called Miracles.
这一集叫做《奇迹》。

453
00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:19.620
And a lot of the things, yes, that was, I am sweating.
而且很多事情，没错，那是，我在出汗。

454
00:20:19.620 --> 00:20:22.340
That was my, the crew was running around furiously
那是我的，工作人员在疯狂地跑来跑去

455
00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:24.580
outside of frame to make that transition happen.
在镜头外面为了完成那个转场。

456
00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:28.940
But, so the thing, I always think it's great
但是，所以，我一直觉得很棒的是

457
00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:31.780
