我们还会聊聊关于这集的许多其他事情，

474
00:21:14.780 --> 00:21:18.180
but I just want to get to this because one of the memories
但我只是想聊这个，因为其中一个回忆

475
00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:21.100
that Marshall has that he says is proof that miracles exist
马歇尔说这是奇迹存在的证据

476
00:21:21.100 --> 00:21:24.420
is this thing that happens where they're throwing pencils
就是发生过这样一件事，他们在麦克拉伦酒吧

477
00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:27.060
up into the ceiling at McLaren's.
把铅笔往天花板上扔。

478
00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:29.700
And one of the pencils falls down from the ceiling,
然后其中一支铅笔从天花板上掉下来，

479
00:21:29.700 --> 00:21:32.420
hits the table and flies up Barney Stinson's nose.
砸在桌子上，然后飞进了巴尼·斯廷森的鼻子里。

480
00:21:32.420 --> 00:21:34.700
Now, one of my favorite categories in this podcast
现在，我在这档播客中最喜欢的环节之一

481
00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:37.900
is the game, can you guess in an episode
就是这个游戏，你能在一集的

482
00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:41.580
of How Much Mother, what's the thing that really happened?
《老爸老妈浪漫史》里猜出哪件事是真实发生的吗？

483
00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:44.460
And I think if you said to someone, watch this episode,
我想如果你对某个人说，看这一集，

484
00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:47.260
it's episode 320, it's a season now of season three,
这是第320集，现在是第三季，

485
00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:50.940
guess the one thing that 100% really happened.
猜一猜那件百分之百真实发生过的事。

486
00:21:50.940 --> 00:21:53.580
I don't think they would guess the pencil up the nose,
我觉得他们绝不会猜到铅笔插进鼻子，

487
00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:56.620
but it is, it really happened.
但它确实发生了，千真万确。

488
00:21:56.620 --> 00:22:01.700
And we have a recording with our very special guest voice,
我们有一段由我们非常特别的特邀嘉宾录制的音频，

489
00:22:01.700 --> 00:22:04.940
voice recording, Chris Harris, the great writer Chris Harris
语音录音，伟大的编剧克里斯·哈里斯

490
00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:09.580
to share his memory of this miracle.
来分享他关于这个奇迹的记忆。

491
00:22:09.580 --> 00:22:11.300
Hey guys, Chris Harris here.
嘿，大家好，我是克里斯·哈里斯。

492
00:22:11.300 --> 00:22:13.220
Thank you for letting me finally tell
谢谢你们让我终于能够讲述

493
00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:16.340
the true story of the miracle of the pencil
关于铅笔奇迹的真实故事

494
00:22:16.340 --> 00:22:18.860
or as the Catholic Church has since christened it,
或者正如天主教会后来命名它的那样，

495
00:22:18.860 --> 00:22:20.740
Miraculum, penicily.
Miraculum penicily。

496
00:22:20.740 --> 00:22:22.180
I know you talked about this a lot.
我知道你们对此讨论了很多。

497
00:22:22.180 --> 00:22:24.180
So much of How Much Mother was based on things
《老爸老妈浪漫史》中很大一部分都基于

498
00:22:24.180 --> 00:22:26.980
that happened to us in real life that we brought into the room.
我们在现实生活中经历并带入编剧室的事情。

499
00:22:26.980 --> 00:22:29.220
But there were two moments from the show
但剧中确实有两个时刻

500
00:22:29.220 --> 00:22:31.180
that came not just from my own life,
不仅仅源自我自己的生活，

501
00:22:31.180 --> 00:22:33.500
but from something that happened to me at work
而是源于我在工作中经历的一件事

502
00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:35.540
while I was in the writer's room.
当时我正在编剧室里。

503
00:22:35.540 --> 00:22:37.020
The second one of those things
这其中的第二件事

504
00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:40.260
became part of season four, episode 16.
成了第四季第16集的一部分。

505
00:22:40.260 --> 00:22:42.820
I'm not going to talk about that one now.
我今天不打算聊那件事。

506
00:22:42.820 --> 00:22:46.140
When we get to season four, episode 16,
等我们说到第四季第16集时，

507
00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:47.980
I am still not going to talk about it
我依然不会聊这件事

508
00:22:47.980 --> 00:22:51.020
because it's not funny and the people think it is funny
因为这事一点也不好笑，但大家都觉得好笑

509
00:22:51.020 --> 00:22:52.900
and I don't want to talk about it, okay?
而我不想聊它，好吧？

510
00:22:52.900 --> 00:22:53.740
Oh, we'll get there.
哦，我们会讲到那里的。

511
00:22:53.740 --> 00:22:56.540
But the pencil incident happened in the second half
但铅笔事件发生在第二季的后半段

512
00:22:56.540 --> 00:22:58.580
of season two and it's very close
而且它和观众最后在节目里看到的

513
00:22:58.580 --> 00:23:01.020
to what people ended up seeing on our show.
非常接近。

514
00:23:01.020 --> 00:23:02.380
So we were all in the writer's room
当时我们全都在编剧室里

515
00:23:02.380 --> 00:23:04.620
sitting around trying to come up with a story
围坐在一起想故事

516
00:23:04.620 --> 00:23:06.620
and we were tossing this large ball around.
我们还在传着一个大球玩。

517
00:23:06.620 --> 00:23:08.980
It's like classic red playground kickball,
就像那种经典的红色操场踢球，

518
00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:10.460
giving each other challenges with it,
大家互相用它出难题，

519
00:23:10.460 --> 00:23:12.500
throw this, catch that, whatever.
抛这个，接那个，诸如此类。

520
00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:15.500
Now the ceiling was this classic tiled office ceiling
当时的天花板是那种经典的办公室格子天花板

521
00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:18.300
and because this had been a writer's room for decades,
而且因为这里做编剧室已经几十年了，

522
00:23:18.300 --> 00:23:20.020
there were a bunch of pencils stuck in it
天花板上插着一堆铅笔

523
00:23:20.020 --> 00:23:21.300
that had been thrown up there.
都是以前被人扔上去的。

524
00:23:21.300 --> 00:23:22.780
Who knows how long they'd been up there?
谁知道它们在那儿待了多久？

525
00:23:22.780 --> 00:23:24.460
Some writer from Mash might have tossed
也许《陆军野战医院》的某个编剧

526
00:23:24.460 --> 00:23:25.700
one of those pencils up.
曾经扔上去过一支呢。

527
00:23:25.700 --> 00:23:28.140
Anyway, Jamie Rohnheimer had the ball
总之，杰米·罗恩海默拿到了球

528
00:23:28.140 --> 00:23:30.140
and I told him, hey, if you throw the ball
我告诉他，嘿，如果你把球扔出去

529
00:23:30.140 --> 00:23:31.740
and knock down one of those pencils,
然后打掉其中一支铅笔，

530
00:23:31.780 --> 00:23:34.460
I can catch both the ball and the pencil.
我能把球和铅笔一起接住。

531
00:23:34.460 --> 00:23:36.100
Everyone was like, okay, let's see it.
大家就起哄说，好啊，让我们瞧瞧。

532
00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:38.180
So he throws the ball up in the air.
于是他把球抛向空中。

533
00:23:38.180 --> 00:23:40.700
It just barely grazes a pencil,
球刚好擦到了铅笔边，

534
00:23:40.700 --> 00:23:42.140
but it doesn't seem to knock it down.
但似乎并没有把它打下来。

535
00:23:42.140 --> 00:23:43.900
Oh, well, so the ball came back down.
好吧，于是球又落了下来。

536
00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:47.260
I caught it in my lap and we all started to move on.
我把它接在腿上，大家正准备继续干别的。

537
00:23:47.260 --> 00:23:49.860
And that's when the pencil came down.
就在这时，铅笔掉下来了。

538
00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:53.020
Suddenly it drops straight down out of the ceiling.
它突然从天花板上笔直地掉了下来。

539
00:23:53.020 --> 00:23:55.220
The eraser of the pencil bounces against
铅笔的橡皮擦撞到了

540
00:23:55.220 --> 00:23:58.020
the rubber red ball and shoots upward like a rocket
红色的橡胶球，像火箭一样向上弹起

541
00:23:58.060 --> 00:24:01.660
point first in a trajectory that just happens
笔尖朝上，其飞行轨迹

542
00:24:01.660 --> 00:24:04.820
to exactly match both the location
刚好完美吻合了

543
00:24:04.820 --> 00:24:08.980
and the angle of my right nostril.
我右鼻孔的位置和角度。

544
00:24:08.980 --> 00:24:12.260
Now, however far you're picturing a pencil shooting up
现在，无论你脑海中想象铅笔插进

545
00:24:12.260 --> 00:24:15.020
into someone's nostril, I want you to double it.
别人鼻孔有多深，我都希望你把它翻倍。

546
00:24:15.020 --> 00:24:16.940
That pencil went way far up.
那支铅笔插得非常深。

547
00:24:16.940 --> 00:24:19.580
Progora was at the computer taking notes at the time.
普罗戈拉当时正坐在电脑前做记录。

548
00:24:19.580 --> 00:24:21.620
He had a perfect side view of the event
他侧面看清了全过程，

549
00:24:21.620 --> 00:24:24.900
and later on he told me, I thought that thing hit brain.
后来他告诉我，我以为那东西扎进脑子里了。

550
00:24:24.900 --> 00:24:26.740
I thought you were dead.
我以为你死定了。

551
00:24:26.740 --> 00:24:28.460
So at this moment, time stops.
所以在这一刻，时间停止了。

552
00:24:28.460 --> 00:24:30.980
The room, the world freezes like inception
房间、整个世界像《盗梦空间》里那样冻结了

553
00:24:30.980 --> 00:24:32.980
or after the gun goes off in Hamilton.
或者像《汉密尔顿》里枪声响过之后那样。

554
00:24:32.980 --> 00:24:37.100
For several full seconds, everyone is just staring at me.
整整好几秒钟，所有人都只是盯着我。

555
00:24:37.100 --> 00:24:38.980
No one moves or says a thing.
没有人动，也没有人说话。

556
00:24:38.980 --> 00:24:40.260
And for me, it was like that moment
对我而言，这就好像那个时刻

557
00:24:40.260 --> 00:24:41.540
right after a bike accident.
自行车事故刚发生的那一刻。

558
00:24:41.540 --> 00:24:45.140
I thought to myself, okay, if I just severely injured myself,
我心想，好吧，如果我刚刚受了重伤，

559
00:24:45.140 --> 00:24:48.540
I'm going to start feeling it right now,
我现在应该就会有感觉了，

560
00:24:48.540 --> 00:24:50.020
but I don't feel anything.
但我什么感觉也没有。

561
00:24:50.020 --> 00:24:54.500
So I quietly say to this frozen room, guys,
于是我对着这个仿佛被按了暂停键的房间轻声说，各位，

562
00:24:54.500 --> 00:24:57.780
I think I'm okay.
我想我没事。

563
00:24:57.780 --> 00:25:02.140
I reach up and I pull the pencil out of my nose.
我把手伸上去，把铅笔从鼻子里面拔了出来。

564
00:25:02.140 --> 00:25:04.460
The tip was slightly broken, but it was intact.
笔尖稍微有点断了，但还算完整。

565
00:25:04.460 --> 00:25:05.940
No evidence of brain.
没有脑浆的迹象。

566
00:25:05.940 --> 00:25:07.740
My hands slowly start to go up in the air.
我的双手慢慢地举了起来。

567
00:25:07.740 --> 00:25:09.620
And then finally, everyone starts cheering.
然后终于，所有人都欢呼起来。

568
00:25:09.620 --> 00:25:11.260
Oh my God, that was amazing.
天哪，太惊艳了。

569
00:25:11.260 --> 00:25:12.940
That's the most insane thing ever.
这是有史以来最疯狂的事。

570
00:25:12.940 --> 00:25:15.700
We can't believe what we've all just been a part of.
我们简直不敢相信自己刚刚经历这一切。

571
00:25:15.700 --> 00:25:18.460
Now, because this had been a TV writer's room in the 80s,
好吧，因为这是80年代的一个电视剧编剧室，

572
00:25:18.460 --> 00:25:20.340
it was probably not the craziest thing
这可能还算不上最疯狂的事

573
00:25:20.340 --> 00:25:22.940
that ever went up anyone's nose in that room.
曾经有人把什么东西塞进鼻子里过。

574
00:25:23.020 --> 00:25:23.980
We didn't care.
我们不在乎。

575
00:25:23.980 --> 00:25:26.020
There was only one word to describe
只有一个词可以形容

576
00:25:26.020 --> 00:25:28.740
what we had all just been a part of.
我们刚才经历的一切。

577
00:25:28.740 --> 00:25:32.740
And that word is miracle.
那个词就是奇迹。

578
00:25:32.740 --> 00:25:33.580
Thanks, guys.
谢谢大家，伙计们。

579
00:25:35.660 --> 00:25:38.740
My God, the great Chris Harris.
天哪，伟大的克里斯·哈里斯。

580
00:25:38.740 --> 00:25:42.060
Craig, you know, we talk a lot about Christmas story
克雷格，你知道的，我们经常谈论《圣诞故事》

581
00:25:42.060 --> 00:25:43.500
being an inspiration.
作为灵感来源。

582
00:25:43.500 --> 00:25:46.140
That was worthy of a Christmas story.
这简直配得上一个《圣诞故事》。

583
00:25:46.140 --> 00:25:48.860
That was like a dream that Jim Shepard could have written
这就像吉姆·谢帕德能写出的梦幻场景

584
00:25:48.860 --> 00:25:50.660
Chris Harris' entire model out there.
克里斯·哈里斯在台上的整套表演。

585
00:25:50.660 --> 00:25:51.500
But which, by the way,
顺便说一句，

586
00:25:51.540 --> 00:25:54.020
Jim performed as acting auditioned class.
吉姆曾在表演试镜课上表演过。

587
00:25:54.020 --> 00:25:55.900
That should now become an audition artiSt.
那现在应该成为一个试镜剧目了。

588
00:25:55.900 --> 00:25:57.580
Take that to the moth, Chris Harris.
把这个带给蛾子剧团吧，克里斯·哈里斯。

589
00:25:57.580 --> 00:25:59.220
That is so good.
真是太棒了。

590
00:25:59.220 --> 00:26:00.220
Spectacular.
叹为观止。

591
00:26:00.220 --> 00:26:01.380
This latest gentleman.
这位最新的绅士。

592
00:26:01.380 --> 00:26:02.900
He has rendered me speechless.
他让我无言以对。

593
00:26:02.900 --> 00:26:03.620
It's so good.
太精彩了。

594
00:26:03.620 --> 00:26:04.460
So it really happened.
所以这真的是发生了。

595
00:26:04.460 --> 00:26:07.100
One of my great regrets in life is that I was not in the room
我人生中最大的遗憾之一就是当时不在那个房间里

596
00:26:07.100 --> 00:26:09.380
when that happened, when I was in editing or on set.
事情发生时，我正在剪辑室或者片场。

597
00:26:09.380 --> 00:26:11.900
And I came back and I was like, what happened?
当我回来的时候，我就问，发生什么事了？

598
00:26:11.900 --> 00:26:14.700
Because there was this electricity in the room.
因为当时房间里充满了电流般的兴奋感。

599
00:26:14.700 --> 00:26:18.180
And they told me this story and it's beyond belief.
然后他们把这个故事告诉我，简直难以置信。

600
00:26:18.180 --> 00:26:21.460
You know, I will say, Chris's line,
你知道，我要说的是，克里斯的台词，

601
00:26:21.460 --> 00:26:24.340
I feel like they beat it when they wrote the show.
我觉得他们在写这个节目的时候就已经超越自我了。

602
00:26:24.340 --> 00:26:25.580
Because Am I Dead?
因为有《我死了吗》？

603
00:26:25.580 --> 00:26:26.180
Am I Dead?
《我死了吗》？

604
00:26:26.180 --> 00:26:28.860
What Barney has said is funnier than I think I'm OK.
巴尼说过的话比我想象的还要搞笑，我觉得我没问题。

605
00:26:28.860 --> 00:26:31.620
Yeah, I thought Am I Dead was dangerous.
对，我觉得《我死了吗》这个梗挺危险的。

606
00:26:31.620 --> 00:26:33.940
I thought Am I Dead was part of the real story.
我以为《我死了吗》是真实剧情的一部分。

607
00:26:33.940 --> 00:26:35.260
But I guess we punched that up.
不过我猜那是我们后来润色加上去的。

608
00:26:35.260 --> 00:26:37.180
I was when Chris shared this memory.
克里斯分享这段记忆的时候，我就在场。

609
00:26:37.180 --> 00:26:39.180
I was like, I can't wait till he says it.
当时我就想，等不及他说出来了。

610
00:26:39.180 --> 00:26:41.100
Am I Dead was we added that, obviously.
《我死了吗》这一句显然是我们后加的。

611
00:26:41.100 --> 00:26:43.500
Am I Dead is really funny.
《我死了吗》真的很好笑。

612
00:26:43.500 --> 00:26:47.260
Now, Pam, how many times I remember from the production meeting.
